# The golden-fixture corpus, one row per line:
#   <fixture-basename> <gallery-program-name>
#
# Single source of truth for which programs have committed snapshot fixtures
# (web/src/__fixtures__/<fixture>.snapshot.json). Read by BOTH
# regen-fixtures.sh (the regen/fix path and the ci.sh drift gate) and the cargo
# golden tests (tests/inspector_goldens.rs), so the two can never disagree
# about the corpus. Keep it bounded — every entry adds regen churn.
#
# The programs are the demo gallery's (`tests/programs/<name>/program.cambra`,
# tabulated in docs/demo-programs.md): the inspector has no example corpus of
# its own, so a program that pins a pane shape is also a program that runs and
# asserts its own value. Selecting a few of those for fixtures is what this
# file does.
#
# A fixture name is the frontend's import path, so it is held stable across a
# program rename — which is why the two columns differ for `arithmetic`.
#
# Every fixture is the full wire. A fixture is a whole payload document, and a
# corpus program whose payload is too large to commit whole belongs in
# tests/inspector_goldens.rs as a structural assertion over a fresh dump
# instead — which is where `txn_multi_read` and `mutation_loop` live.
#
# A program added for backend coverage alone needs NO row here: ratchet 5 of
# tests/inspector_goldens.rs already walks every gallery source through the
# wire validator.
arithmetic udf_closure
polymorphic polymorphic
list_min list_min
# A deliberate type error -> the degraded (payloadKind: "failed") payload.
failed type_error
# inline fan-out (RT-3): Derived(Inline) copies + post-inference -> post-channelize edges.
udf_fanout udf_fanout
# UDF-of-defer: try_lift_defer fires, lifted feed head keeps its id (RT-5).
defer_lift defer_lift
